body:
@williammartin I believe this should now be ready for maintainer review :)

Regarding changes to the prompt about the CONTRIBUTING.md guidelines, I suppose you mean the content of the automated comment, right? I'd suggest including it explicitly in the PR template as well — and if you'd allow me the slight digression, I would also appreciate if the template was written in a way that would make sense if an actual human is filling it out.

Specifically, I was a little uncertain in a few aspects, e.g. whether I could omit the "Key points" and "Notes for reviewers" sections if empty; also, in the "Authorship and follow-up" section, the references to @username + "Name the account" felt a little awkward and unclear. I ended up adding a note underneath the checklists since none of the options reflected how I used AI for this change.
